# netsurf: crypto.subtle -- digest (SHA-1/256/384/512) and HMAC (patch 215)
# Generated 2026-10-07
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser d431979 (patch stack through 214)
#
# crypto.subtle was undefined (one of the API census' 5 missing), so
# OAuth 2.1 / PKCE sign-in -- which sends base64url(SHA-256(verifier)) --
# failed or fell back, as did libraries hashing for integrity checks and
# cache keys. vita_polyfill.js now provides, in pure JS:
#  - digest() for SHA-1, SHA-256, SHA-384, SHA-512;
#  - HMAC over those: importKey('raw', ..., {name:'HMAC', hash}),
#    sign('HMAC'), verify('HMAC') (constant-time compare), exportKey('raw')
#    for extractable keys; a CryptoKey global;
#  - every other method (encrypt, decrypt, generateKey, deriveKey,
#    deriveBits, wrapKey, unwrapKey) rejects with NotSupportedError, which
#    pages treat as "this browser cannot".
# As in browsers it exists only in a secure context (https:, file:,
# localhost / 127.0.0.1 / [::1]); results are Promises of ArrayBuffers.
# The hashes were checked against Node's crypto for every length 0-399
# (all four) and HMAC with 5-, 64- and 150-byte keys over lengths 0-300
# (688 + 1600 cases, 0 mismatches) before going in.
#
# Test: testpages/pages/JS-crypto-subtle.html (SUBTLE215, 5 checks,
# Chromium 5/5; crypto.subtle absent without the patch): presence,
# SHA-256/SHA-1/SHA-512 of "abc" (FIPS 180 vectors), RFC 4231 case 2
# HMAC-SHA-256 with verify, the RFC 7636 appendix B PKCE challenge.
# tools/run-vita-sim.sh's API census floor goes 149 -> 172.
